VideoToolbox sessions keep their V4L2 buffers in guest memory (USERPTR), not in crosvm's media_host pool (MMAP): the
pool is shared once at boot and two 4K decoders (the lock screen's video and its still) outgrew 128 MiB. Each buffer is wired kernel
memory of the size QUERYBUF gives, and its pages go to the device as virtio-media's scatter list after the v4l2_buffer of every
QBUF: DroidVMVirtioMedia.c's droidvm_media_ioctl_sg puts the list in a descriptor of its own after the payload.

